      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability: removing unused imports and constants, extracting magic numbers as named constants, and adding clarity to the loop logic.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports and the unused `UTF_16` constant, extracts magic numbers (`128`, `64`) into named constants with explanatory comments, renames `offset` to `totalBytesVerified` for clarity, and adds Javadoc comments to both helper methods explaining their purpose and the two-path (constructor vs. builder) strategy."
